Z||000000||87GTZ34||02-15-2001||04:05 PM||||Has anyone changed the torsion rods for the decklid on a V6 with the eng in?  Haven't scoped it out yet just checking.||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||02-15-2001||06:29 PM||||Yes, you will need a length of pipe that will fit over the rod and blocks of wood.<P>Read the factory manual. Very important, but yes I've done it several times.<P>The issue is not getting them out, it's not breaking the rear window.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||02-15-2001||10:02 PM||||Thanks Terry.  You're right about the window... I took the rods out of F#1 (w/o the engine and used a piece of plywood and 2x4 block.  I just wanted to find out from someone that changed them with eng in, and I'm sure it's a whole lot more fun.<P>thanks again,<P>Ron||||reg||1
